      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nordheim began in 1895 as the railway siding Weldon Switch on the San Antonio and Aransas Pass line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordheim%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A year later, 1896, the town was renamed Nordheim after the German town of Baden-Württemberg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordheim%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Nordheim Brass Band, founded in 1902, remained Texas’s oldest continuously active German ensemble until it disbanded after 1972.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
